{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"agent_message","text":"The vendor path remains decisively best for large matrices, but `M=4` now has a second win (about 15.5 µs versus 19.8 µs). For the `M=14–80` cluster, the bottleneck is too few tiles, so I’m testing split-K: independent FP32 partial GEMMs followed by one compact FP32 reduction-and-FP16-store kernel. This increases CU occupancy while preserving the required accumulation precision."}}
